---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Baroque Karaoke" description="A participatory performance system that turns any sentence into baroque karaoke, sung by six historical figures.">
  <article class="project">

    <header class="project-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">interactive systems · 2026</span>
      <h1 class="display-xl project-title">Baroque Karaoke</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="hero-video">
      <video
        class="hero-vid"
        poster="/images/baroque-karaoke/hero-loop-poster.jpg"
        autoplay
        loop
        muted
        playsinline
      >
        <source src="/images/baroque-karaoke/hero-loop.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
    </div>

    <div class="project-body">

      <p class="lead">
        Baroque Karaoke takes a sentence about nothing — a broken coffee machine, a missed appointment — and asks a language model to perform it as tragedy. Six historical figures, six eras, one system prompt swapping tone for grandeur. The banality doesn't disappear into the baroque frame. It sits inside it, still banal, now singing.
      </p>

      <hr class="type-divider" />

      <p>
        This started as a search for an AI interaction that felt fun, not just technically impressive. I wanted the AI to make something happen, not just make something. Karaoke kept resurfacing — an ordinary sentence, transformed into something performative enough to invite participation. The user doesn't read the output. They sing it. Consuming becomes performing — that shift is the whole project.
      </p>

      <p>
        From there, the AI stopped being a text generator and started being a performer. Historical characters, theatrical personalities, a Hype Man mode — all ways of giving it presence. Not a chatbot. Someone trying to entertain a room, improvising, occasionally stealing the spotlight. Baroque Karaoke names what it became: excess, ornamentation, spectacle. Not karaoke. Karaoke with delusions of grandeur.
      </p>

      <p>
        The system runs on three variables recombined at every performance: character, drama, and the sentence itself. A dropdown swaps Shakespeare for Napoleon for Aristotle — swaps the portrait, the era, the voice injected into the prompt. A slider called Drama moves the tone instruction from quiet dignity to operatic overwroughtness. The sentence stays exactly as banal as it was typed. GPT-4o-mini doesn't fix that. It performs it.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        The banality doesn't disappear into the baroque frame. It sits inside it, still banal, now singing.
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        Underneath, seven modular containers in TouchDesigner handle input, prompt construction, the API call, lyric parsing, word timing, and the final composite — a brass plaque UI, a gilt frame, neon cyan text that pulses word by word over an oil-painted landscape. A Tempo slider controls scroll speed after generation; Temperature controls how far the model wanders before it. Failure is part of the design: a missing API key doesn't crash the piece, it turns the portrait red and asks you to try again.
      </p>

      <div class="image-pair">
        <div class="project-image">
          <img
            src="/images/baroque-karaoke/marie-antoinette-performance.jpg"
            alt="Marie Antoinette performing 'I spent all day waiting and nobody showed up'"
            class="content-img"
            onerror="this.style.display='none'"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="project-image">
          <img
            src="/images/baroque-karaoke/aristotle-performance.jpg"
            alt="Aristotle performing 'The coffee machine is broken and I have not slept'"
            class="content-img"
            onerror="this.style.display='none'"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        The project isn't a demonstration of generative AI. It's AI as performer — the technology isn't the artwork, it's the engine that turns language into a shared moment between the user and the machine.
      </p>

      <div class="section-divider">
        <span class="eyebrow">the pipeline</span>
      </div>

      <div class="project-image">
        <img
          src="/images/baroque-karaoke/system-architecture-diagram.svg"
          alt="Baroque Karaoke system pipeline — seven containers from input to visual composite"
          class="content-img"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="project-meta">
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span class="meta-label eyebrow">year</span>
        <span class="meta-value">2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span class="meta-label eyebrow">medium</span>
        <span class="meta-value">interactive systems / participatory performance</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span class="meta-label eyebrow">tools</span>
        <span class="meta-value">TouchDesigner · OpenAI API (GPT-4o-mini) · Python</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span class="meta-label eyebrow">collaborators</span>
        <span class="meta-value">Solo</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--page-padding-x) var(--space-8);
  }

  .project-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .project-title {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .hero-video {
    background: var(--surface);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    min-height: 340px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero-vid {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .project-body {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }
  .lead {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-weight: var(--w-light);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--mid);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .type-divider {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }
  p {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--w-light);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--mid);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .section-divider {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .project-image {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .content-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .image-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }
  .image-pair .project-image {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .project-meta {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .meta-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-2) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .meta-label {
    color: var(--gold);
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }
  .meta-value {
    font-weight: var(--w-light);
    color: var(--mid);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .project {
      padding: var(--space-5) var(--page-padding-x-sm) var(--space-7);
    }
    .image-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .meta-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
